### 10. Noncompliance, suspension and termination

**10.1 Operational conditions.** The qualifying burn and evidence requirements
are express conditions limiting permission for Live Deployment. They are not
merely optional reporting commitments.

A Live Deployment without the qualifying burn coverage required at the time of
operation is outside the permission granted by this License.

**10.2 Suspension.** Permission to operate an affected Live Deployment is
suspended immediately when qualifying burn coverage is insufficient or when a
required reconciliation remains incomplete beyond its deadline.

The affected deployment must not resume operational use until the applicable
requirements have been satisfied.

Subsequent compliance does not retrospectively authorize earlier noncompliant
operation.

**10.3 Administrative correction.** Where the required qualifying burns
occurred on time but a record contains an inadvertent documentary error, the
operator may correct that error within thirty (30) days after discovering it
or receiving written notice, whichever occurs first.

This correction period does not permit an unbacked deployment, concealment of
a burn shortfall, deliberate misrepresentation or continued operation
following a substantive funding failure.

**10.4 Material or deliberate violations.** Deliberate evasion, material
falsification of evidence or repeated intentional breach terminates the
responsible operator's permissions under this License in relation to the
affected use and material.

Reinstatement following such termination requires express written
authorization from the relevant Copyright Holders.

**10.5 Independent rights.** Termination does not invalidate previously
acquired rights under independent licenses, the Organization's express rights
under Section 7, or the permissions of independently compliant recipients.

The remedies and liabilities available to Copyright Holders are determined by
applicable law. Nothing in this License creates an automatic monetary penalty
or permits recovery beyond what applicable law allows.

